  "safety": [
    "Touching the two terminals to metal, or to each other in a pocket or drawer, can short-circuit the battery and cause heat or fire; tape the terminals of loose 9V batteries before disposal.",
    "Do not mix chemistries, brands or charge states in one device.",
    "Only NiMH, NiCd and USB-rechargeable lithium-ion 9V packs are designed to be recharged; charging alkaline, zinc-carbon or lithium (Li-MnO2) 9V batteries can cause leakage or rupture."
  ],
  "notes": "The 9V format is the only household size with snap terminals. IEC 6LR61 is for alkaline and 6F22 for zinc-carbon; the Energizer 522 sheet lists both 6LF22 and 6LR61. Wikipedia lists PP3 as the Ever Ready name from the PP (Power Pack) series.",
